id: pm-script-launch-evidence
title: "Review1608: classify absent script interpreters and make negative controls replayable"
description: "Review1608 identified an executable script whose shebang interpreter is absent. A successful command lookup is insufficient proof that the script started. Conservatively corroborate native shell startup diagnostics with the resolved script header and absent absolute interpreter, retaining raw result data and child assertions. Clarify exact pre-fix adapter revisions and replay commands for lifecycle recovery negative controls without rewriting immutable history."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T02:42:14.362Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T03:35:46.839Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T03:35:45.818Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-27T03:35:45.818Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A real POSIX script with a missing interpreter fails as spawn_error while retaining platform exit code and stderr; Installed scripts deliberately emitting matching diagnostics or exiting127 remain assertion failures and commands are never rerun during classification; Lifecycle guidance negative controls explicitly pin the failing adapter revision and replay only the relevant assertion in an isolated tracker
parent: pm-gh1604
resolution: Classify independently verified missing POSIX script interpreters with canonical absence semantics and preserve native results. Make all three pinned regression replays reject suite-level runtime errors using actual Vitest4 testResults messages. Preserve historical evidence and record the current hosted source receipt.
expected_result: "Missing interpreters classify conservatively without rerunning user commands, and replay proof accepts only its intended assertion failure with empty suite error messages."
actual_result: "All three corrected pinned-source replays prove exactly their intended AssertionError. Current production/test source8bed passes every required hosted check, native Windows, six packed first-run legs and exact aggregate100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts.111 linked tests, Node/Bun consumers, and local static/governance acceptance pass. Final metadata-only head checks and review remain mandatory before merge."
